Added `dub publish` command.

Registers a package repository with the DUB registry from the command line
(default action), or checks status / triggers a metadata refresh.

Previously registration required submitting a repository URL through the
website after logging in. `dub publish` automates that flow using session
login (`POST /login`) and `POST /register_package`.

-------
# credentials via environment (preferred in CI)
export DUB_REGISTRY_USER=myname
export DUB_REGISTRY_PASSWORD=secret

# register the current package's git origin remote
dub publish

# check whether a package exists
dub publish status -n vibe-d

# queue a metadata refresh (after pushing a SemVer tag)
dub publish update -n mypkg --secret YOUR_PACKAGE_SECRET
-------

Use `--annotate` for a dry run. Credentials may also be stored under the DUB
settings directory with `--save-credentials`.
